# Monthly backup of sensitive files to the 1Password vault Backups
# (sd:10098), on the hub only: its profile's .cron names it. The files
# come from <config>/sensitive-backup/targets; local-sensitive-backup has
# the example and the rules.
#
# op signs in as a service account that can write only to Backups. Its
# token is OP_BACKUP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN in ~/.config/shell/env.sh, which
# the runner loads before this command; the command maps it to
# OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN for this run alone, so no other op call in a
# shell acts as the service account. An empty token fails the run before
# op starts: with app integration op waits for Touch ID, and an unattended
# run timed out. The variable is escaped so the `bash -c` reads it.
#
# 03:40 on the 1st, past the 02:xx slot, since op needs the network.
# Dashboard Management's Run now runs it by hand; a second run in a month
# replaces that month's item.
JOB_SCHEDULE="40 3 1 * *"
JOB_TIMEOUT="30m"
JOB_COMMAND="OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN=\"\${OP_BACKUP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN:-}\" sh \"$ROOT/../local-sensitive-backup/sensitive-backup.sh\" run"
